description:
pkix-ct/src/lib.rs:6-40

The crate-level rustdoc lists what is implemented but does not show
the caller workflow:

> SCT binary-format parsing ... is implemented; see
> `SignedCertificateTimestamp` and `SctList`. Delivery-channel
> adapters ... see `sct_list_from_tls_extension` and ...
> `sct_list_from_ocsp_response`. CT log list management is
> implemented behind ... see `CtLog`, `CtLogList`, and
> `CtLogList::from_google_log_list_json`. SCT signature
> verification ... see `verify_sct_for_cert` and
> `verify_sct_for_precert`. Merkle inclusion proof verification
> ... see `verify_inclusion` and `verify_sth`.

This reads as a feature checklist, not a usage guide. The caller
who wants to verify CT for a TLS server has to discover, in order:

1. Parse SCTs from `Certificate.tbs_certificate.extensions[sct_oid]`
   via `SctList::from_extension_value`.
2. Or for OCSP: `sct_list_from_ocsp_response`.
3. Or for TLS handshake: `sct_list_from_tls_extension`.
4. Get a log list:
   `CtLogList::from_google_log_list_json(fetch(GOOGLE_URL))`.
5. Build verifier: `SctVerifier::new(log_list, DefaultVerifier)`.
6. For embedded SCTs (precert_entry):
   `verify_embedded_scts(leaf, issuer)` or per-SCT
   `verify_sct_for_precert(sct, leaf, issuer)`.
7. For OCSP / TLS handshake SCTs (x509_entry): per-SCT
   `verify_sct_for_cert(sct, cert)`.
8. Check the count against your policy threshold (BR §3.2.2.9).

That 8-step pipeline is in the maintainer's head but not on the
page.

Recommendation: add a `# Usage` section to lib.rs (after the
existing `# Limitations` section, perhaps renamed `# Status`).

```rust
//! # Usage
//!
//! To verify CT compliance for a TLS server cert:
//!
//! ```no_run
//! use pkix_ct::{SctList, SctVerifier, CtLogList};
//! use pkix_path::DefaultVerifier;
//!
//! // Step 1 — log list (caller-supplied trust state).
//! let logs = CtLogList::from_google_log_list_json(json)?;
//! let verifier = SctVerifier::new(logs, DefaultVerifier);
//!
//! // Step 2 — verify embedded SCTs.
//! let n = verifier.verify_embedded_scts(leaf_cert, issuer_cert)?;
//! assert!(n >= 2, "CA/B Forum TLS BR §3.2.2.9 minimum");
//!
//! // Step 3 — optionally verify Merkle inclusion proofs.
//! // ...
//! # Ok::<(), pkix_ct::Error>(())
//! ```
```

Priority P3 because the information is technically available; this
makes the contract accessible. Similar treatment in `pkix-chain`'s
README (which I checked earlier) makes a big difference for caller
onboarding.
